IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa24-officers`
IMPORT `coa24-penalty`
IMPORT `coa24-register`

-- coa24-tests-register.l4: tests for ss 1092C to 1098 (coa24-register.l4). Expected values were decided from the text
-- before the run. Dates are worked out by hand; the pounds are test figures that stand for nothing.

§ `Test figures`

`the test amounts` MEANS `s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments` WITH
    `s 1125 level 1 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 100
    `s 1125 level 2 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 200
    `s 1125 level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 300
    `s 1125 level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 400
    `s 1125 level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 500
    `s 1125 the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS 1000

`the test amounts with a large level 4` MEANS `s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments` WITH
    `s 1125 level 1 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 100
    `s 1125 level 2 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 200
    `s 1125 level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 300
    `s 1125 level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 8000
    `s 1125 level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 500
    `s 1125 the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS 1000

`the test amounts with level 4 at exactly 5000` MEANS `s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments` WITH
    `s 1125 level 1 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 100
    `s 1125 level 2 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 200
    `s 1125 level 3 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 300
    `s 1125 level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 5000
    `s 1125 level 5 on the standard scale, in pounds` IS 500
    `s 1125 the statutory maximum, in pounds` IS 1000

`a director who permitted the contravention` MEANS `s 1121(3) conduct of the officer` WITH
    `s 1121(3) authorises or permits` IS TRUE
    `s 1121(3) participates in` IS FALSE
    `s 1121(3) fails to take all reasonable steps to prevent` IS FALSE

`a director who did nothing wrong` MEANS `s 1121(3) conduct of the officer` WITH
    `s 1121(3) authorises or permits` IS FALSE
    `s 1121(3) participates in` IS FALSE
    `s 1121(3) fails to take all reasonable steps to prevent` IS FALSE

§ `Tests for s 1092C`

-- (2): subsection (1) applies to any offence other than the listed ones.
#ASSERT `s 1092C(2) subsection (1) applies to the offence` `s 1092C(2)(a)(i) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1092C(2) subsection (1) applies to the offence` `s 1092C(2)(a)(ii) an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1092C(2) subsection (1) applies to the offence` `s 1092C(2)(a)(iii) an offence under section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1092C(2) subsection (1) applies to the offence` `s 1092C(2)(a)(iv) an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1092C(2) subsection (1) applies to the offence` `s 1092C(2)(a)(v) an offence under section 32 or 32A of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1092C(2) subsection (1) applies to the offence` `s 1092C(2)(a)(vi) an offence under section 34 or 35 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1092C(2) subsection (1) applies to the offence` `s 1092C(2)(b) any other offence, not within paragraph (a), an element of which is the delivery to the registrar of a document, or the making of a statement to the registrar, that is misleading, false or deceptive` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1092C(2) subsection (1) applies to the offence` `s 1092C(2) any other offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1): the statement may not be used against the person where it was made in response to a requirement under s 1092A.
#ASSERT `s 1092C(1) the statement may not be used against the person in the criminal proceedings` TRUE `s 1092C(2) any other offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1092C(1) the statement may not be used against the person in the criminal proceedings` TRUE `s 1092C(2)(a)(i) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1092C(1) the statement may not be used against the person in the criminal proceedings` TRUE `s 1092C(2)(b) any other offence, not within paragraph (a), an element of which is the delivery to the registrar of a document, or the making of a statement to the registrar, that is misleading, false or deceptive` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1092C(1) the statement may not be used against the person in the criminal proceedings` FALSE `s 1092C(2) any other offence` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1092C(1) the statement may not be used against the person in the criminal proceedings` FALSE `s 1092C(2)(a)(i) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for s 1093`

#ASSERT `s 1093(1) the registrar may give notice to the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1093(1) the registrar may give notice to the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1)(a) and (b): a notice that states the respects and requires resolution within the period is a notice of the kind described.
#ASSERT `s 1093(1)(a)-(b) the notice is a notice of the kind subsection (1) describes` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1093(1)(a)-(b) the notice is a notice of the kind subsection (1) describes` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1093(1)(a)-(b) the notice is a notice of the kind subsection (1) describes` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1)(b): the period of 14 days beginning with the day of issue ends 13 days after it.
#ASSERT `s 1093(1)(b) the last day of the period for resolving the inconsistency` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 14 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 1093(1)(b) the last day of the period for resolving the inconsistency` (Date 20 3 2026) EQUALS Date 2 4 2026
#ASSERT `s 1093(1)(b) the last day of the period for resolving the inconsistency` (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS Date 13 1 2027

#ASSERT `s 1093(2) the notice meets the requirement of s 1093(2)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1093(2) the notice meets the requirement of s 1093(2)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (3)(a): notice issued 1 March 2026, so the period runs 1 to 14 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 1093(3)(a) the company commits an offence` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1093(3)(a) the company commits an offence` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Delivered on the last day of the period (14 March): no offence.
#ASSERT `s 1093(3)(a) the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 14 3 2026)) (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Delivered on the day of issue: no offence.
#ASSERT `s 1093(3)(a) the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 3 2026)) (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Delivered one day late (15 March): the documents were not delivered within the period, so an offence is committed.
#ASSERT `s 1093(3)(a) the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not delivered, asked on the last day: the period has not yet ended, no offence yet.
#ASSERT `s 1093(3)(a) the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 14 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not delivered, asked the day after: an offence is committed.
#ASSERT `s 1093(3)(a) the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- (3)(b): every officer of the company who is in default also commits it.
#ASSERT `s 1093(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) `s 1121(2)(a) a director` `a director who permitted the contravention` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1093(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) `s 1121(2)(a) a director` `a director who did nothing wrong` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1093(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 14 3 2026)) (Date 15 3 2026) `s 1121(2)(a) a director` `a director who permitted the contravention` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1093(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) `s 1121(2) none of these positions` `a director who permitted the contravention` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1093(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) `s 1121(2)(a) a director` `a director who permitted the contravention` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4): both versions of the daily default fine are encoded; the text does not choose.
#ASSERT `s 1093(4) the punishment for the offence under subsection (3)` `s 1093(4) the text read as one-tenth of level 5` `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1), `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
-- Second version: one-tenth of the greater of 5,000 and level 4. With level 4 at 400 the greater is 5,000, so 500 a day.
#ASSERT `s 1093(4) the punishment for the offence under subsection (3)` `s 1093(4) the text read as one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4` `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` OF 500), `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
-- With level 4 at 8,000 the greater is 8,000, so 800 a day.
#ASSERT `s 1093(4) the punishment for the offence under subsection (3)` `s 1093(4) the text read as one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4` `the test amounts with a large level 4` EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` OF 800), `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
-- Where level 4 is exactly 5,000 the two amounts are equal and the greater is 5,000: 500 a day.
#ASSERT `s 1093(4) the punishment for the offence under subsection (3)` `s 1093(4) the text read as one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4` `the test amounts with level 4 at exactly 5000` EQUALS JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` OF 500), `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
-- The text does not say which version applies: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 1093(4) the punishment for the offence under subsection (3)` `s 1093(4) the text does not say which version applies` `the test amounts` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative rule for the same duty (s 1093(1)(b), (3)): the clock counts days from the day of issue (day 0).
-- Delivered on day 13 (14 March when issued 1 March): FULFILLED. Delivered on day 14: late, BREACH. Never delivered: BREACH.
-- These traces are read from the run, not asserted: a DEONTIC value cannot be compared in #ASSERT on this binary.
#TRACE `s 1093(3) the company's duty to deliver the necessary documents` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 1093(3) the company` DOES `s 1093(3) deliver the necessary documents to the registrar` AT 13

#TRACE `s 1093(3) the company's duty to deliver the necessary documents` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 1093(3) the company` DOES `s 1093(3) deliver the necessary documents to the registrar` AT 14

#TRACE `s 1093(3) the company's duty to deliver the necessary documents` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 14)

§ `Tests for s 1094`

#ASSERT `s 1094(1) the registrar may remove the material from the register` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1094(1) the registrar may remove the material from the register` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1094(1) the registrar may remove the material from the register` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1094(1) the registrar may remove the material from the register` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Whether the material is unnecessary material is section 1074's answer: not supplied, and not a document under section 1073: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 1094(1) the registrar may remove the material from the register` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1094(1) the registrar may remove the material from the register` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 1094(2) the power to remove material may be exercised` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1094(2) the power to remove material may be exercised` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1094(2) the power to remove material may be exercised` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3): material whose registration had legal consequences: only if satisfied that the interest in removal outweighs.
#ASSERT `s 1094(3) the registrar may exercise the power to remove the material` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1094(3) the registrar may exercise the power to remove the material` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1094(3) the registrar may exercise the power to remove the material` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1094(3) the registrar may exercise the power to remove the material` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1) and (3) together: appears-to-be, legal consequences, satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 1094(1) and (3) the registrar may remove the material from the register` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1094(1) and (3) the registrar may remove the material from the register` FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1094(1) and (3) the registrar may remove the material from the register` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1094(1) and (3) the registrar may remove the material from the register` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1094(1) and (3) the registrar may remove the material from the register` FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1094(1) and (3) the registrar may remove the material from the register` FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1094(1) and (3) the registrar may remove the material from the register` FALSE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

