§ `Tests for ss 1097A, 1097B and 1097C`

#ASSERT `s 1097A(5)(a) the regulations may provide for a suspension of this length` 28 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1097A(5)(a) the regulations may provide for a suspension of this length` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1097A(5)(a) the regulations may provide for a suspension of this length` 29 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 28 days beginning with the day of registration: 5 February 2026 + 27 days is 4 March 2026 (February 2026 has 28 days).
#ASSERT `s 1097A(5)(a) the last day of a suspension of 28 days` (Date 5 2 2026) EQUALS Date 4 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 1097A(5)(a) the last day of a suspension of 28 days` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 28 3 2026

-- Level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, one-tenth of level 3.
#ASSERT `s 1097A(4A)(a) the punishment for a summary offence in the regulations` EQUALS Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING, `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 0.1), `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1097B(6) the punishment for a summary offence in the regulations` EQUALS `s 1097A(4A)(a) the punishment for a summary offence in the regulations`
#ASSERT `s 1097C(6) the punishment for a summary offence in the regulations` EQUALS `s 1097A(4A)(a) the punishment for a summary offence in the regulations`
-- The same punishment, measured with s 1125: on a second conviction, 3 days: one-tenth of level 3 (test figure 300) is 30 a day, so 90.
#ASSERT `s 1125(2) the most the person can be fined on this conviction, in pounds` `s 1097A(4A)(a) the punishment for a summary offence in the regulations` TRUE 3 `the test amounts` EQUALS JUST 90

